// ── :feature:* ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// UI layer — one module per functional context.
// Contains ONLY Composables, ViewModels (MVI pattern), and
// internal navigation. Features never talk to :data:* directly;
// all business operations go through UseCases from :domain:*.
// Features never import each other — communication happens
// through the navigation graph in :composeApp.
//
// MVI pattern enforced per screen:
//   UiState   → immutable snapshot of what the UI shows
//   Intent    → sealed class of user actions / events
//   ViewModel → maps Intents → updates UiState via StateFlow
//
// Internal structure (same pattern for every :feature:* module):
//   ui/
//     XxxScreen.kt              → root Composable, observes UiState
//     components/
//       XxxComponent.kt         → reusable sub-composables for this feature
//   viewmodel/
//     XxxViewModel.kt           → holds StateFlow<XxxUiState>, handles XxxIntent
//   model/
//     XxxUiState.kt             → data class with all UI state fields
//     XxxIntent.kt              → sealed class of user actions
//     XxxSideEffect.kt          → one-time events (navigation, toasts)
//   navigation/
//     XxxNavGraph.kt            → internal routes for this feature
//   di/
//     XxxFeatureModule.kt       → DI bindings (ViewModel, UseCase injection)
//
// Depends on  : :domain:*, :shared:design-system, :core:common
// Must NOT import : :data:*, another :feature:*, :core:network, :core:database